<title>FRANCE: EU traders expect wheat refund near 16-17 Ecus.</title>
<headline>EU traders expect wheat refund near 16-17 Ecus.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>European grain traders said on Thursday they expected the European Union to award wheat export refunds of between 16 and 17 Ecus per tonne at the weekly tender to allow them to carry out existing contracts.</p>
<p>But while apparently breaking a previous price link with the United States, such a refund would not be adequate to let them compete directly with Argentina and Australia, they said.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals committee is meeting in Brussels to decide whether to accept traders' bids for subsidies that would peg EU wheat prices below U.S. ones for the first time in months.</p>
</text>
